# LOTA EK manufacturer trust sources -- template.
#
# Copy this to `sources` and add one line per certificate the fleet's EK
# certificates chain through. scripts/lota-ek-roots-update.sh refuses a file
# with no line, as an unedited copy is.
#
#   <sha256>  <filename>  <class>  <url>  <vendor label...>
#
#   sha256    hex SHA-256 over the certificate DER. Take it from the vendor
#             out of band, never from the download: the script refuses a
#             certificate whose fingerprint differs from it.
#   filename  bare name the certificate is written under in the bundle.
#             The CA loads any name the manifest lists; a .pem file the
#             manifest does not name makes it refuse the bundle.
#   class     `root` for a self-signed manufacturer root, which anchors a
#             chain, or `intermediate` for a certificate the CA builds a
#             path through but never anchors at.
#   url       https address the script fetches the certificate from.
#   label     free text, written to the bundle manifest.
#
# The script refuses a file with no root line. Every CA certificate on the
# path that the TPM does not carry itself needs an intermediate line: a TPM
# that keeps the certificates nearest its EK in NV (0x01c00100) has the agent
# send them with the enrollment request, and only the ones above them come
# from the bundle. scripts/lota-ek-root-pin.sh walks an EK certificate to its
# root and prints a candidate line for the root and each certificate it
# fetched, with pins that still need checking against the vendor.
#
# Reading an EK certificate from the TPM:
#
#   sudo tpm2_nvreadpublic                       # find the 0x01c0xxxx EK cert
#   sudo tpm2_nvread 0x01c00002 -o ek.der        # RSA EK (0x01c0000a = ECC)
#   openssl x509 -in ek.der -inform DER -noout -issuer -ext authorityInfoAccess
#
# An EK certificate with no Authority Information Access names no issuer to
# fetch; read the certificates above it from NV first and pass them on:
#
#   sudo tpm2_nvread 0x01c00100 -o nvchain.bin
#   scripts/lota-ek-root-pin.sh --nv-chain nvchain.bin ek.der
#
# Example lines; a pin that is not 64 hex characters, such as <sha256>,
# is refused:
#
# <sha256>  vendor-root.pem  root          https://pki.example/r.crt  Root
# <sha256>  vendor-int.pem   intermediate  https://pki.example/i.crt  Int
